The official patch *AC-15210* did not properly patch the `getAllowedMethods()` call in Carrier Model, which causes issues with other extensions, such as the Amasty Shipping Restrictions extension.

Here is a patch which fixes this issue:

```diff
diff --git a/vendor/magento/module-usps/Model/Carrier.php b/vendor/magento/module-usps/Model/Carrier.php
index 058a0384..14fabb55 100644
--- a/vendor/magento/module-usps/Model/Carrier.php
+++ b/vendor/magento/module-usps/Model/Carrier.php
@@ -1251,10 +1379,20 @@ class Carrier extends AbstractCarrierOnline implements \Magento\Shipping\Model\C
      */
     public function getAllowedMethods()
     {
-        $allowed = explode(',', $this->getConfigData('allowed_methods') ?? '');
         $arr = [];
-        foreach ($allowed as $k) {
-            $arr[$k] = $this->getCode('method', $k);
+
+        if ($this->isXmlRequest()) {
+            $allowed = explode(',', $this->getConfigData('allowed_methods') ?? '');
+
+            foreach ($allowed as $k) {
+                $arr[$k] = $this->getCode('method', $k);
+            }
+        } else {
+            $allowed = explode(',', $this->getConfigData('rest_allowed_methods') ?? '');
+
+            foreach ($allowed as $k) {
+                $arr[$k] = $this->getCode('rest_method', $k);
+            }
         }

         return $arr;
```

I've included this in my backported [Magento v2.4.5-p14 patch](https://gist.github.com/jaywilliams/97ca39652b917e95f22e1d29c85bb466).

I've been working through the v3 migration for a different stack and hit the same wall. A few things that might help people here while Adobe works on the official fix:

**Why tracking is broken:** AC-15210 swapped the USPS base URL to `apis.usps.com/tracking/v3/` but `_parseTrackingResponse()` still calls `simplexml_load_string()` on the response. The v3 API returns JSON, not XML — so it silently fails and shows "tracking not found." The fix is replacing the XML parser with `json_decode()` and mapping the new response fields (`trackingEvents` array instead of `<TrackDetail>` nodes).

**Why you're hitting 429s:** The v3 API enforces ~60 requests/hour by default (the old Web Tools API had no practical limit). AC-15210 requests a fresh OAuth token on *every single API call* instead of caching it. Each token is valid for 8 hours, so you're burning through your rate limit on auth calls alone. Here's the fix:

```php
// Cache the OAuth token in Magento's cache backend
$cached = $this->cache->load('usps_oauth_v3_token');
if ($cached) {
    return $cached; // No HTTP call needed
}

// Only fetch when cache is empty
$response = $this->httpClient->post('https://apis.usps.com/oauth2/v3/token', [
    'grant_type' => 'client_credentials',
    'client_id' => $clientId,
    'client_secret' => $clientSecret,
    'scope' => 'addresses tracking prices',
]);
$data = json_decode($response);

// Cache with 30-min buffer before expiry
$this->cache->save($data->access_token, 'usps_oauth_v3_token', [], $data->expires_in - 1800);
return $data->access_token;
```

**Rate field mapping:** The v3 pricing endpoint returns `mailClass: "PRIORITY_MAIL"` and `totalBasePrice` — different from the old `<MailService>Priority Mail</MailService>` and `<Rate>` XML structure. If your allowed methods config references the old service names, rates come back empty.

**Requesting higher limits:** You can email USPS at their Web Tools inquiry form (https://emailus.usps.com/s/web-tools-inquiry) to request a rate limit increase. They do grant them for production applications.

I wrote up the full breakdown of what AC-15210 changes and what it misses here: https://revaddress.com/blog/magento-usps-ac15210-fix — includes the field mapping table and a drop-in token caching module.

The rate limit architecture is covered separately: https://revaddress.com/blog/usps-api-rate-limits-2026-what-changed

@warmoth-dev @cod62627 

Here's the updated `processShippingRateForItem()` method in the *Model/ShipmentService.php*, which incorporates a fix for Priority Mail International quotes. _(Note the added preg_match() call)_

``` php
    /**
     * Processing rate for ship element
     *
     * @param array $rateElement
     * @param array $costArr
     */
    private function processShippingRateForItem(
        array $rateElement,
        array &$costArr
    ): void {
        if (empty($rateElement['productName']) && empty($rateElement['description'])) {   
            return;
        }
        $productName = $rateElement['description'];

        // Standardize international service names
        if (preg_match('/Priority Mail( Express)? International (Nonstandard|Machinable) ISC Single-piece/', $productName, $matches)) {
            $productName = "Priority Mail" . ($matches[1] ?? '') . " International ISC Single-piece";
        }

        $methodCode = strtoupper(substr($this->replaceSpaceWithUnderscore($productName), 0, 120));
        $methodTitle = $this->shippingMethodManager->getMethodTitle($methodCode);
        $allowedMethods = $this->getRestAllowedMethods();
        if (in_array($methodCode, array_keys($allowedMethods))) {
            // Use totalPrice if available, otherwise use price
            $cost = isset($rateElement['totalPrice']) ?
                (float)$rateElement['totalPrice'] : (float)$rateElement['price'];
            $costArr[$methodCode] = [
                'price' => $cost,
                'code' => $methodCode,
                'productName' => $methodTitle
            ];
        }
    }

```

I also updated the `getJsonQuotes()` method with a minimum Postal Code/ZIP limit, to reduce the number of unnecessary API requests. *(Note the different minimums for US/International addresses)*

```php
           if ($this->carrierModel->_isUSCountry($request->getDestCountryId())) {
                $requestParam['destinationZIPCode'] = is_string($request->getDestPostal()) ?
                    substr($request->getDestPostal(), 0, 5) : '';

                // Skip API request if ZIP code is incomplete
                if (strlen(trim($requestParam['destinationZIPCode'])) < 5) {
                    return $this->_parseJsonResponse([]);
                }
            } else {
                $requestParam['destinationCountryCode'] = $request->getDestCountryId();
                $requestParam['foreignPostalCode'] = $request->getDestPostal() ?? '';

                // Skip API request if postal code is incomplete
                if (strlen(trim($requestParam['foreignPostalCode'])) < 3) {
                    return $this->_parseJsonResponse([]);
                }
            }
```

All of these fixes have been included in my backported AC-15210 patch for Magento v2.4.5-p14.
https://gist.github.com/jaywilliams/97ca39652b917e95f22e1d29c85bb466

Hope that helps others out there with this rough Magento USPS rollout.

The following patch will fix the 1lb issue, where products weighting less than 1lb do not have the USPS shipping options at checkout. 

```
diff --git a/vendor/magento/module-usps/Model/ShipmentService.php b/vendor/magento/module-usps/Model/ShipmentService.php
index 02ccf7da..cee26b47 100644
--- a/vendor/magento/module-usps/Model/ShipmentService.php
+++ b/vendor/magento/module-usps/Model/ShipmentService.php
@@ -204,8 +204,14 @@ class ShipmentService
         ];

         foreach ($request->getPackages() as $packageData) {
+            
+            $weight = isset($packageData['weight_pounds']) && $packageData['weight_pounds'] > 0
+                ? (float) $packageData['weight_pounds']
+                : (float) ($packageData['weight_ounces'] ?? 16) / 16;
+        
             $requestParam['packageDescription'] = [
-                "weight" => $packageData['weight_pounds'] ?? 1,
+                // "weight" => $packageData['weight_pounds'] ?? 1,
+                "weight" => $weight,
                 "mailClass" => 'ALL'
             ];
             $requestParam['packageDescription']['length'] = $request->getLength() ? (int) $request->getLength() : 1;
```

Note that you first need to patch the USPS module using the quality patches tool, then apply the patch above. To enforce the correct sequence of patches, you can use the following in composer.json:

```
    "scripts": {
        "post-install-cmd": [
            "./vendor/bin/magento-patches apply AC-15210",
            "@apply-custom-patches"
        ],
        "post-update-cmd": [
            "./vendor/bin/magento-patches apply AC-15210",
            "@apply-custom-patches"
        ],
        "apply-custom-patches": [
            "patch -p1 < patches/composer/module-usps-sub-1-pound-weight.patch"
        ]
    }
```

Additional note - if you have a list of existing patches in your composer.json under 'extra', then they will execute first, followed by the quality patches AC-15210, and finally the module-usps patch above

