I can also confirm that if you have multiple stores the `hasSpecialPrice()` function in `\Magento\Catalog\Pricing\Render\FinalPriceBox` is broken and returns nothing/false when the storeId != the website ID.

I am not sure why you are looking up pricing from `catalog_product_index_price` which is keyed on websiteId by storeID.

@engcom-November @engcom-Bravo this is easily reproducible if you add another store

Using this patch, I was able to fix the issue.
You can map it in the composer.json like this:
```
"extra": {
        "magento-force": "override",
        "patches": {
            "magento/module-catalog": {
                "ACP2E-4100: Regular price is not visible, even though a special price is applied (SpecialPriceBulkResolver fix)": "patches/ACP2E-4100-special-price-bulk-resolver.patch"
            },
        }
}
``` 

[ACP2E-4100-special-price-bulk-resolver.patch](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26264351/ACP2E-4100-special-price-bulk-resolver.patch)

I'd add an additional check on top of the [ACP2E-4100-special-price-bulk-resolver.patch](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26264351/ACP2E-4100-special-price-bulk-resolver.patch) patch:
```
--- a/vendor/magento/module-catalog/Pricing/Render/FinalPriceBox.php	2026-03-26 11:51:19
+++ b/vendor/magento/module-catalog/Pricing/Render/FinalPriceBox.php	2026-03-26 11:53:55
@@ -158,7 +158,7 @@
                 return false;
             }

-            return (bool)$this->getData('special_price_map')[$this->saleableItem->getId()];
+            return (bool)($this->getData('special_price_map')[$this->saleableItem->getId()] ?? false);
         } else {
             $displayRegularPrice = $this->getPriceType(Price\RegularPrice::PRICE_CODE)->getAmount()->getValue();
             $displayFinalPrice = $this->getPriceType(Price\FinalPrice::PRICE_CODE)->getAmount()->getValue();
